WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.180
- You have a 16-month-old, right?

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:02.013
- Yeah, I do, yeah.

00:00:02.013 --> 00:00:02.880
- That, I mean, okay.

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.270
And you just started on a new show,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.103
which we're gonna talk about.

00:00:05.103 --> 00:00:05.950
But here's the thing.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:09.200
I felt like I went to work
too early with my first one,

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:10.850
and it was exhausting.

00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:12.150
- It was exhausting, yeah.

00:00:12.998 --> 00:00:14.460
- You started five months after, right?

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.560
- I started five months after,

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.070
but just acting is exhausting.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:18.430
It's not like,

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:19.550
I don't know, it just takes

00:00:19.550 --> 00:00:21.520
all of your mental capacity, kind of.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.450
Like, I cried to my
mother-in-law week two,

00:00:23.450 --> 00:00:24.980
'cause she came to help me,

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:26.810
and I was just, "I don't
know how I'm gonna do this."

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.490
- You just cried in week two?
- I just cried.

00:00:28.490 --> 00:00:29.750
I was like, "I can't do this."

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:30.807
- I cried, like, every week.

00:00:30.807 --> 00:00:32.443
(audience laughs)

00:00:32.443 --> 00:00:33.434
It was week two for you.
- But before that,

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:34.534
I just was home.

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:35.760
I just stayed home.

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.870
But now recently,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:40.120
like when he turned 10
months I got help finally,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.460
because I have a weird job, you know.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.590
I'm, like, home all the time,

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.670
but I also have to read and
do other things during the day

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:46.000
so I can't--
- Or you're gone all the time.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.430
- Or I'm gone, yeah.

00:00:47.430 --> 00:00:49.290
But now I got my own wife, I realize.

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:51.300
Like, having a nanny's like having a wife.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.547
I'm like, "This is the best thing

00:00:53.547 --> 00:00:54.950
"on the planet Earth."

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:55.800
I was like, "Bye.

00:00:57.274 --> 00:00:59.280
"Have fun."
- She's safe and happy, bye.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:01.590
- She's cooking an amazing
pesto dish for him.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.210
This kid eats better than I
have ever eaten in my life.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.820
- Oh my God, she's a chef too?

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:06.820
- Yeah, she does it all.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.110
- Your kid lucked out, all right.

00:01:08.110 --> 00:01:10.360
- He really did, He's spoiled
- I love that.

